  <li><a href="#annexure">Annexure</a></li>
</ul>

<!-- ======================== EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ====================== -->
<h1 id="executive-summary">Executive Summary</h1>
<p>{{Client.Name}} engaged {{CompanyName}} to conduct a Black Box Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) of its application{{#if Engagement.Title}} ({{Engagement.Title}}){{/if}}.
This security assessment was performed from an external attacker's perspective, without prior knowledge of the application's internal architecture, source code, or credentials.</p>
<p>The engagement was carried out from {{formatDate Engagement.StartDate}} to {{formatDate Engagement.EndDate}}. The primary objective was to evaluate the current security posture of {{Client.Name}} and identify externally exploitable security vulnerabilities.</p>
{{{text Report.ExecutiveSummary}}}

<h1 id="summary-of-findings" class="continue">Summary of Findings</h1>
<p>The assessment identified a total of {{numberWords Counts.Total}} distinct vulnerabilities across all assessed areas of {{Client.Name}}'s application.{{#if Counts.Total}} The chart below shows the vulnerabilities and their severity found within the application infrastructure.{{/if}}</p>
{{#if Counts.Total}}
<p>Among the various types of vulnerabilities found in the systems and services, {{severityBreakdown Counts}} during our test{{#if Engagement.Title}} within the {{Engagement.Title}} application{{/if}}.</p>
<div class="figure"><img src="{{SeverityChart}}" alt="Vulnerabilities by Severity" style="width:150mm" data-word-width="560"></div>
{{/if}}

<h1 id="key-findings" class="continue">Key Findings</h1>
{{{text Report.KeyFindings}}}

<h1 id="key-recommendations" class="continue">Key Recommendations</h1>
{{{text Report.KeyRecommendations}}}


<!-- Scope of Engagement sits under Key Recommendations, as in the SELISE Black Box sample. -->
<div class="keep-together">
<h2 id="scope">Scope of Engagement</h2>
<h3>Detailed Scope of Work</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Application</th><th>Attack Vector</th><th>URL / Target</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  {{#each Scope}}
  <tr><td>{{Application}}</td><td>{{AttackVector}}</td><td>{{Url}}</td><td>{{Status}}</td></tr>
  {{else}}
  <tr><td colspan="4">{{#if ../Engagement.Scope}}{{../Engagement.Scope}}{{else}}Scope as agreed with the client.{{/if}}</td></tr>
  {{/each}}
</table>
</div>

<!-- ========================== INTRODUCTION ========================= -->
<h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>

<h2 id="methodology">Methodology for Security Assessment</h2>
<div class="figure"><img src="{{asset "black-flow.png"}}" alt="Black Box assessment flow" style="width:165mm" data-word-width="600"></div>
<p>At {{CompanyName}}, our Black Box Security Assessment methodology is designed to evaluate the security posture of an application from an external attacker perspective. The assessment is conducted without prior knowledge of the application's internal architecture, source code, or credentials, simulating real-world attack scenarios. This approach helps identify externally exploitable vulnerabilities, security misconfigurations, and weaknesses that could be leveraged by malicious actors to compromise the application.</p>

<h2 id="limitations">Limitations</h2>
{{{text Report.Limitations}}}

<h2 id="discovered-vulnerabilities">Discovered Vulnerabilities</h2>
<p>The assessment identified a total of {{numberWords Counts.Total}} distinct vulnerabilities.{{#if Counts.Total}} Among these, {{severityBreakdown Counts}}.{{/if}} The list of vulnerabilities is as follows:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Vulnerability</th><th>Severity</th><th>Vulnerable Systems</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  {{#each Findings}}
  <tr><td>{{Title}}</td><td class="sev-{{Severity}}">{{Severity}}</td><td>{{Occurrences}}</td><td>{{Status}}</td></tr>
  {{else}}
  <tr><td colspan="4">No vulnerabilities were identified within the assessed scope.</td></tr>
  {{/each}}
</table>

<!-- ======================== DETAILED FINDINGS ====================== -->
<h1 id="detailed-findings">Detailed Findings</h1>
{{#each Findings}}
<div class="finding">
  <h2 id="{{Anchor}}">{{Id}} — {{Title}}</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><td class="label">Finding ID</td><td>{{Id}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">Severity</td><td class="sev-{{Severity}}">{{upper Severity}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">CVSS Score</td><td>{{#if CvssScore}}{{CvssScore}}{{#if CvssVector}} ({{CvssVector}}){{/if}}{{else}}—{{/if}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">Affected System</td><td>{{AffectedSystem}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">Vulnerable Endpoint</td><td>{{Endpoint}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">Tools Used</td><td>{{ToolsUsed}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">References</td><td>{{#each References}}{{this}}<br>{{else}}—{{/each}}</td></tr>
    <tr><td class="label">Status</td><td>{{Status}}</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h3>Description</h3>
  {{{text Description}}}
  {{#if AiExplanation}}{{{text AiExplanation}}}{{/if}}
  {{#if Impact}}<h3>Impact</h3>{{{text Impact}}}{{/if}}
  <h3>Recommendations</h3>
  {{#if Recommendation}}{{{text Recommendation}}}{{else}}<p>Remediate according to vendor guidance and secure coding best practices.</p>{{/if}}
  {{#if ProofOfConcept}}<h3>Proof of Concept</h3><div class="code">{{ProofOfConcept}}</div>{{/if}}
  {{#each Screenshots}}
  <div class="figure"><img src="{{DataUri}}" alt="Evidence" style="max-width:165mm" data-word-width="600">{{#if Caption}}<p class="caption">{{Caption}}</p>{{/if}}</div>
  {{/each}}
  {{#if StepsToReproduce}}<h3>Steps of Reproduction</h3>{{{text StepsToReproduce}}}{{/if}}
</div>
{{else}}
<p>No vulnerabilities were identified within the assessed scope.</p>
{{/each}}

<!-- ============================ ANNEXURE =========================== -->
<h1 id="annexure">Annexure</h1>
<h2>Vulnerability Scoring</h2>
<h3>Risk Scoring Methodology</h3>
<p>To ensure a consistent and standardized assessment of identified vulnerabilities, risk ratings are based on the Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) v3.1. CVSS evaluates the severity of vulnerabilities by considering factors such as exploitability, potential impact, and environmental context, providing a reliable framework for prioritizing remediation efforts.</p>
<p>The CVSS scoring system is categorized as follows:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>CVSS (v3.1) Score</th><th>Severity Level</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>0.0</td><td class="sev-Informational">Informational</td><td>No security risk, but may indicate misconfigurations, best practices, or system information leakage.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>0.1 – 3.9</td><td class="sev-Low">Low</td><td>Minimal impact; requires high privileges or user interaction.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>4.0 – 6.9</td><td class="sev-Medium">Medium</td><td>Potential data leakage or privilege escalation, limited scope.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>7.0 – 8.9</td><td class="sev-High">High</td><td>Unauthorized access, remote exploitation, or system compromise.</td></tr>
  <tr><td>9.0 – 10.0</td><td class="sev-Critical">Critical</td><td>Full system compromise, remote execution, or widespread impact.</td></tr>
</table>

